{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":true}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Secradow","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/secradow.webp","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/secradow.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Secradow","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":115,"temp":0,"max":115,"details":""},"ac":{"value":25,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"resistances":[{"type":"void","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","elven","shadowtongue"],"details":""},"level":{"value":7},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Secrets weigh heavily on the souls of mortals, and sometimes this weight is so powerful that it can be felt even on the Shadow Plane. When this happens, the secret's ripple effect on the Shadow Plane can grow and transform into a secradow, taking on an appearance and knowledge similar to the creature who felt the secret's weight, though the secret twists the secradow's shadowy image slightly, giving clues to its true nature.</p>\n<p>Secrets can only survive by staying hidden, so a secradow does all it can to stay that way. It single-mindedly hunts down and destroys all evidence of its secret's existence, caring little about anything else.</p>\n<p>Coming into existence on the Shadow Plane does cause a secradow some problems though, as it doesn't have any inherent ability to move between planes. For this reason, a secradow usually finds another creature that can shift between planes and uses whatever means necessary to gain passage to the Material Plane so it can protect its secret.</p>\n<h2>Crushing Weight</h2>\n<p>An unspoken romantic attraction can create a conflicted secradow whose existence depends upon fostering the interest while dissuading impulses to act on it. Such a secradow may impersonate the crush to lead its creator on, constructing an elaborate web of lies to support the emotional affair.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 45/100/180 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Deception, Lore [Secret], Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> dexterity, energy resistant (negative, positive), strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Garry Stacey Johnston","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":6},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"exposure sense","mod":15,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{